                        "review": "[h3]Basically FTL as an arcade action shooter with simplified mechanics. Absolutely beautiful but not exactly my kind of roguelite structure. Fun to play for a few runs but gets repetitive.[/h3]\n\nEverspace is absolutely stunning to look at. The combat is super smooth and the story is kind of good with not-that-good voice acting.\n\nThat being said, I don't think this game really works as a roguelite for me. RNG doesn't do a good job giving you a unique experience each run, making the game feel repetitive very quickly. Runs can easily take 2+ hours which is a considerable time commitment and I didn't really feel much of a power creep between the start of a run and the end which is definitely something I look for in roguelites.\n\nHad fun with it working towards my first clear but unless you're REALLY into the gameplay loop and are fine with runs playing out the same way-ish each time, I don't think this'll be a game you'll want to replay over and over again which is unfortunate for a roguelite.",
